        "original_id": "5b375487-709e-52a4-9440-f01883b4aa8f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Brooklyn Dodgers, St. Louis Cardinals\n- People: Clyde Kluttz\n- Events: 1946 National League tie-breaker series, 1946 World Series\n- Topics: 1946 Brooklyn Dodgers season\n\nFacts:\n- The 1946 Brooklyn Dodgers finished the regular season tied for first place with the St. Louis Cardinals.\n- The Brooklyn Dodgers and the St. Louis Cardinals both finished the 1946 regular season with identical 96–58 records, which made the 1946 National League tie-breaker series necessary.\n- Clyde Kluttz appeared in 52 regular season games for the 1946 world champion St. Louis Cardinals.\n- On October 3, Clyde Kluttz was the starting catcher for the St. Louis Cardinals in the flag-clinching Game 2 of the postseason playoff against the Brooklyn Dodgers.\n- Clyde Kluttz did not play in the 1946 World Series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1c6de532-3b31-5939-b01d-6dc793dcade2",
        "text": "Page: 1946 National League tie-breaker series. Sentence: It was necessary after both teams finished the season with identical win–loss records of 96–58.\nPage: 1946 Brooklyn Dodgers season. Sentence: The 1946 Brooklyn Dodgers finished the season tied for first place with the St. Louis Cardinals.\nPage: Clyde Kluttz. Sentence: Kluttz appeared in 52 regular season games as a member of the world champion Cardinals—and was the starting catcher on October 3 for the flag-clinching Game 2 of the postseason playoff against the Brooklyn Dodgers—but he did not play in the 1946 World Series.",
